Given an array of integers nums containing n + 1 integers where each integer is in the range [1, n] inclusive.

There is only one repeated number in nums, return this repeated number.

You must solve the problem without modifying the array nums and uses only constant extra space.



 int findDuplicate(vector<int>& nums) {
     
      for(int i=0;i<nums.size();i++){
          
        int indx = abs(nums[i]);
          
        if(nums[indx]<0)
            return indx;
          
          nums[indx] = -nums[indx];
          
      }
        
        return nums.size();
        
    }
    
    
    ****************************************************************************************************************************************************************
    since there are n+1 integers and numbers vary from 1 to n . Then each can represent a index in the array. now if we take the first element it can be anything 
    from 1 to n. then it represents a certain position in the array , we negate that position's value.then if we find that element again and go to it's pointing loca
    tion then we will find that negated number . this is the only caase when there is a duplicate element and none else.
